/**
 * @mainpage pulsatrix
 *
 * **ExAI-first C++ deep learning library** — explainability as a first-class property of the
 * computation graph, not a post-hoc wrapper. Every relevance-bearing layer ships a real,
 * cited, conservation-tested Layer-wise Relevance Propagation (LRP) rule alongside its
 * forward/backward math — never a placeholder or a post-hoc explainer bolted on afterward.
 *
 * This page is the Doxygen API reference's landing page — generated from `include/`'s doc
 * comments only. For guides, worked examples, and build instructions, see the full
 * [documentation site](https://joshuaweg.github.io/pulsatrix/) and the
 * [GitHub repository](https://github.com/Joshuaweg/pulsatrix).
 *
 * @section mainpage_modules Modules
 *
 * - @ref dl_modules — Tensor/autograd core, layers, optimizers, losses, device backends
 * - @ref interpretability — post-hoc explainers (@ref interpretability_lrp,
 *   @ref interpretability_agnostic, @ref interpretability_dl) and explanation-quality checks
 * - @ref rl — environments, agents, and RL training algorithms
 * - @ref mech_interp — activation probing, sparse autoencoders, circuit graphs, GFlowNets
 * - @ref neuro_symbolic — differentiable fuzzy logic, a Datalog engine, and a neural-predicate
 *   bridge tracing relevance from a symbolic derivation back into the network
 * - @ref data_pipeline — dataset/loader/transform core and per-modality datasets
 * - @ref evolutionary — genetic algorithms, neuroevolution, evolutionary HPO, PBT, E-GAN
 * - @ref hyperparameter_optimization — search space, Bayesian optimization, bandit-based
 *   early stopping
 * - @ref visualization — JSON documents and SVG figures (always built), plus opt-in Dear
 *   ImGui + ImPlot dashboards (`PULSATRIX_ENABLE_VIZ`)
 * - @ref system_monitoring — CPU/GPU utilization, memory and temperature logging
 *
 * @section mainpage_start Where to go next
 *
 * - [Getting Started](https://joshuaweg.github.io/pulsatrix/getting-started/) — build the
 *   library and run your first example.
 * - [Recipes](https://joshuaweg.github.io/pulsatrix/recipes/) — small, runnable programs
 *   demonstrating one tool at a time.
 */
